      "message": "[From Jetski review] Calling s.as_static_mut() twice in the same assignment statement creates two aliasing \u0026\u0027static mut Self references simultaneously (while the \u0026\u0027static FrozenModule borrow from the RHS is live, the LHS creates a second \u0026\u0027static mut Self), which violates Rust\u0027s aliasing rules. Also, s is a stack-allocated value that gets moved when returned on line 70. Since FileLoader::preload already pins the module on the heap and calls extend_lifetime(\u0026*pinned) internally, if FileLoader::preload returns \u0026\u0027static FrozenModule directly (or if we only extend_lifetime the reference returned by s.loader.preload), we can avoid as_static_mut(\u0026mut self) altogether.",
