      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: Using `as_static_mut` here creates overlapping mutable references to the local variable `s` (since both the receiver for `loader` and `builtin_rules` evaluate to `\u0026mut s` in the same expression), which is undefined behavior. Additionally, returning `s` immediately invalidates those `\u0027static` references.\n\nIf `extract_builtin_rules` is changed to take `\u0026FrozenModule` instead of `\u0026\u0027static FrozenModule`, you can avoid this UB entirely:\n\n```rust\n        let mut s \u003d Self {\n            loader: Default::default(),\n            path_resolver,\n            globals: build_globals(),\n            targets: Default::default(),\n            builtin_rules: Vec::new(),\n        };\n        s.builtin_rules \u003d rule::extract_builtin_rules(s.loader.preload(\n            Label::parse(\"//builtins:rules.scl\", PackageRef::root()).unwrap(),\n            rule::register_builtin_rules::\u003ccrate::eval_context::EvalContext\u003e(),\n        ));\n        s\n```",
