      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T05:39:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: There are a couple of safety/UB issues here:\n1. `std::ptr::NonNull::dangling().as_ref()` is immediate undefined behavior because it creates a reference to unallocated/unaligned memory, even if it\u0027s never dereferenced. Use `Option` for the placeholder.\n2. Taking `\u0026\u0027static FrozenModule` forces callers to do unsafe lifetime transmutations. Since the rules are allocated on a `FrozenHeap` that outlives the targets referencing them, you can accept a temporary `\u0026FrozenModule` and extend the lifetime of the rules internally instead.\n\n```rust\npub fn extract_builtin_rules\u003cC: EvalContextAttrExt\u003e(\n    module: \u0026FrozenModule,\n) -\u003e Vec\u003cOption\u003c\u0026\u0027static Rule\u003c\u0027static, C\u003e\u003e\u003e {\n    let mut rules \u003d Vec::new();\n    rules.push(None);\n    for output_type in OutputType::iter() {\n        assert!(rules.len() \u003d\u003d output_type as usize);\n        let rule \u003d module\n            .get_option_ref(\u0026output_type.to_string())\n            .unwrap()\n            .unwrap()\n            .value()\n            .downcast_ref::\u003cRule\u003c\u0027static, C\u003e\u003e()\n            .unwrap();\n        rules.push(Some(unsafe { std::mem::transmute(rule) }));\n    }\n    rules\n}\n```",
